+    write_json(a.output_dir/f'{prefix}_audit.json', dict(phase='development_exploratory',confirmation_authorized=False,attempts=attempts,authorized_roots={t:AUTHORIZED[t] for t in tasks},runs=run_rows,read_errors=errors,statistics='descriptive only; no p-values, significance, seed pooling, winner or checkpoint selection',tables=tables))
+    write_json(a.output_dir/f'{prefix}_confirmation_draft.json',dict(status='not_authorized',confirmation_authorized=False,selected_candidate=None,primary_comparison=None,freeze_complete=False,required_before_authorization=['validation-only selection record or explicit no-go','full protocol and comparison family freeze','failure floor and exclusion rules','capacity/FLOPs and complete query budgets','environment/code/config/data hashes','task feasibility and input-isolation acceptance','second author approval'],confirmation_roots_accessed=False))
+    included=sum(r['included'] for r in rows)
+    report=f'''# Exploratory development audit\n\nExplicit attempts: `{json.dumps(attempts,ensure_ascii=False)}`. Included completed method-root runs: {included}/{len(rows)}. JSON read errors: {len(errors)}.\n\nOnly the nine authorized development roots can be read. No confirmation data are opened. This report neither selects a winner nor changes metrics. With at most three independent root seeds per task, all summaries are descriptive: no significance claims, p-values, confirmatory confidence intervals, or pooling of tasks. Test episodes and gradient probes do not increase the seed count.\n\nBase-extra-data NMSE uses common-plus-extra training scales, whereas other model methods use common-train scales. Raw NMSE remains reported, but cross-method NMSE differences involving base_extra_data are null and marked noncomparable; this is not a same-denominator comparison.\n\nDirect FD/SPSA need no world-model checkpoint or gradient-fidelity metric; those fields are not applicable, not zero. Their optimizer stop reason and actual/reserved query counts are retained.\n\nMissing, failed, smoke and invalid runs remain visible; excluded outcomes are null. Complete methods in an otherwise failed attempt remain available unless the attempt is explicitly invalid. NaN/undefined metrics remain null; no unregistered failure floor is invented. Available-case means report their missing count and must not conceal incomplete evidence. Failure records and resource costs remain in the audit.\n\nThe raw table separates development-test outcomes from validation metrics. Missing validation physical returns or gradient cosine prevent the protocol's validation-only selection rule from being evaluated; development-test metrics cannot substitute. Protocol acceptance gates, contact reachability/full-episode success and vision isolation require separate actual logs. A positive local reward or cosine does not establish complete-task success.\n\nD/R/G use the eight ff/delay/recurrent/combined Base/Dir cells, excluding frozen legacy methods. Main effects average four differences; D×R averages the two difference-in-differences. Any missing cell leaves that seed's effect undefined. Only tracking full-coordinate cosine is the protocol's proposed confirmation mechanism endpoint; all present factorial estimates are exploratory. Capacity controls compare exact trainable counts against combined_dir and flag ±5%; missing FLOPs remain unverified. Return gains without cosine gains do not support gradient fidelity, and correlations would not establish mediation.\n\nPAML is a deterministic-actor/observable-interface adaptation, not an original-paper reproduction. VaGraM is an inspired value-state-gradient weighting adaptation; critic fit, representation assumptions, extra parameters and resource/query costs require disclosure. Privileged information is not a fair deployable comparison or a mathematical upper bound.\n\nResource CSV preserves actual logged scopes. Wall times are elapsed wall time; CUDA-event elapsed time is **not GPU-active kernel time**, utilization or hardware energy. Peak allocation/reservation are measured memory peaks, not additive usage. Nested stage/method/attempt times overlap and must not be summed. Shared critic/visual/data costs are separate; absent per-method attribution, physics-substep counts, FLOPs or failure-phase GPU timing are unknown, never zero. Budget CSV records actual available control-step categories; common-data comparisons do not imply equal total query budgets or cost-effectiveness. Unrequested attempts are not scanned, so historical failure totals require separate explicit analysis.\n\nConfirmation draft status: **not_authorized**. No candidate is populated and no confirmation run is launched.\n'''
+    (a.output_dir/f'{prefix}_report.md').write_text(report)
+    print(json.dumps(dict(report=str(a.output_dir/f'{prefix}_report.md'),included_method_roots=included,read_errors=len(errors))))
+
+
+if __name__ == '__main__':
+    main()
